# Git branch and PR naming (Jira)

When creating a git branch or pull request, use the Jira ticket if one is available.

## Clean the summary first

From the Jira summary, drop:

- Bracket prefixes such as `[FE]`, `[BE]`, `[Agent<->FE Bug]`
- Text before the first `|` (for example `B2BCF|`)

Keep the remaining title as-is (do not lowercase it).

Example ticket: `COP-6002 B2BCF|FE Agent in streaming mode`  
Cleaned name: `FE Agent in streaming mode`

## Branch name

`{TICKET}-{cleaned-name-in-kebab-case}` — spaces become hyphens; keep original word casing.

```
COP-6002-FE-Agent-in-streaming-mode
```

## Pull request title

`{TICKET} {cleaned name}` — ticket, space, cleaned summary (not kebab-case).

```
COP-6002 FE Agent in streaming mode
```

## If there is no Jira ticket

Use a short kebab-case branch and a plain-language PR title. Do not invent a ticket key.
